---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About Us - Tap Tempo | ttaptempo.com"
  description="Discover the story and engineering behind ttaptempo.com. Built by audio engineers and musicians to deliver an ultra-fast, zero-latency, 100% free online tap tempo and metronome tool."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <!-- Breadcrumbs -->
    <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400 mb-6">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-neutral-900 dark:hover:text-neutral-100 transition-colors">Home</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span class="text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 font-medium">About Us</span>
    </nav>

    <!-- Header Badge & Title -->
    <div class="mb-10">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-blue-500/20 bg-blue-500/10 text-xs font-mono text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 mb-4">
        <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-blue-500"></span>
        <span>Audio Engineering &amp; Timing Tools</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-50 mb-3">
        About ttaptempo.com
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 max-w-2xl">
        We build minimalist, developer-grade audio utilities designed for studio musicians, touring performers, beatmakers, and music educators worldwide.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Main Content -->
    <article class="prose prose-neutral dark:prose-invert max-w-none text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base space-y-10">
      
      <!-- Section 1: The Origin Story -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-3">
          Why We Built ttaptempo.com
        </h2>
        <p>
          Whether you are tracking drums in a recording studio, synchronizing delay repeats on a pedalboard before a gig, or DJing a live festival transition, finding the exact tempo of music should take seconds—not minutes.
        </p>
        <p>
          Unfortunately, most existing web tools built in the 2000s were never modernized: they are covered in pop-up banner ads that block the tap button, require slow full-page reloads, fail to work reliably on mobile touchscreens, or trap essential features behind mandatory account registrations and monthly subscriptions.
        </p>
        <p>
          We created <strong>ttaptempo.com</strong> with a clear, uncompromising mandate: <strong>craft the fastest, cleanest, most mathematically accurate tap tempo and metronome tool on the web</strong>—completely free, ad-sensible, and without any sign-up walls.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Feature Grid: Pillars -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 not-prose my-6">
        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 bg-white dark:bg-neutral-900 shadow-xs">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-emerald-500/10 text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm mb-3">
            01
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-base text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-1">100% Free Forever</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
            No trial periods, no paywalls, no "pro" tiers. All features—from audio metronomes to the delay sync table—are unconditionally open to everyone.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 bg-white dark:bg-neutral-900 shadow-xs">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm mb-3">
            02
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-base text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-1">Zero Accounts or Tracking</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
            No username, no password, no email collection. Simply navigate to the URL and start tapping immediately.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 bg-white dark:bg-neutral-900 shadow-xs">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-purple-500/10 text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm mb-3">
            03
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-base text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-1">Sub-Millisecond Timing</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
            Utilizes hardware-accelerated high-resolution microsecond timers to calculate accurate rolling averages and eliminate human tapping jitter.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 bg-white dark:bg-neutral-900 shadow-xs">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-amber-500/10 text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm mb-3">
            04
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-base text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-1">Synthesized Web Audio</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
            Pure in-browser oscillator and noise-burst sound generation with zero sample download delay, perfect downbeat accents, and multiple sound kits.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Section 2: Technical Engineering -->
      <div class="pt-6 border-t border-neutral-100 dark:border-neutral-900">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-3">
          The Engineering Behind Our Tools
        </h2>
        <p>
          Behind the minimalist visual interface lies a robust audio engineering pipeline built on modern web standards:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
          <li>
            <strong>High-Resolution Interval Capture:</strong> We measure inter-tap intervals using <code class="font-mono text-xs">window.performance.now()</code>, which provides timing resolution down to thousandths of a millisecond.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Weighted Rolling Average Algorithm:</strong> Human tapping naturally fluctuates by 10–25 milliseconds. Our smoothing algorithm filters out anomalous single-tap spikes and computes a rolling 16-tap window to yield rock-solid BPM readings within ±0.1 BPM.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Drift-Free Audio Metronome:</strong> Standard JavaScript <code class="font-mono text-xs">setInterval</code> is subject to CPU throttling and tab desynchronization. We implement a lookahead audio scheduler driven by the Web Audio API hardware clock, guaranteeing sample-accurate clicks without timing drift.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Zero-Lag Mobile Haptics:</strong> On touch devices supporting the HTML5 Vibration API, tapping the pad triggers micro-vibrations for a tactile, physical pad feel.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- Section 3: Who Uses Our Tools -->
      <div class="pt-6 border-t border-neutral-100 dark:border-neutral-900">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-3">
          Who Uses ttaptempo.com?
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-500 mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">Music Producers &amp; Beatmakers:</strong>
              <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 mt-0.5">
                Quickly discover the tempo of sample loops or vocal acapellas before importing them into Ableton Live, FL Studio, Logic Pro, or Cubase.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-blue-500 mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">Guitarists &amp; Pedalboard Enthusiasts:</strong>
              <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 mt-0.5">
                Calculate exact millisecond delay times (1/4 note, dotted 1/8 note, triplets) to dial in Strymon, Boss, Line 6, or TC Electronic delay pedals.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-purple-500 mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">DJs &amp; Live Performers:</strong>
              <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 mt-0.5">
                Verify unanalyzed vinyl records or live band tempo in real time during live venue sets.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-amber-500 mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">Music Students &amp; Educators:</strong>
              <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 mt-0.5">
                Study classical Italian tempo markings (Andante, Allegro, Presto) and train rhythmic muscle memory.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Section 4: Tested & Calibrated -->
      <div class="pt-6 border-t border-neutral-100 dark:border-neutral-900">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-3">
          Studio Calibration &amp; Testing
        </h2>
        <p>
          Our timing equations and delay tables are calibrated against industry-standard digital audio workstations (DAWs) and laboratory hardware metronomes to ensure our math matches commercial studio environments:
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 not-prose my-3">
          <span class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-50 dark:bg-neutral-900 text-xs font-mono text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">Ableton Live 12</span>
          <span class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-50 dark:bg-neutral-900 text-xs font-mono text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">Apple Logic Pro</span>
          <span class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-50 dark:bg-neutral-900 text-xs font-mono text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">Avid Pro Tools</span>
          <span class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-50 dark:bg-neutral-900 text-xs font-mono text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">FL Studio</span>
          <span class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-50 dark:bg-neutral-900 text-xs font-mono text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">Strymon Timeline</span>
          <span class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-50 dark:bg-neutral-900 text-xs font-mono text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">Boss DD-500</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Section 5: Contact & Feedback CTA -->
      <div class="pt-6 border-t border-neutral-100 dark:border-neutral-900">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-3">
          Get in Touch With Us
        </h2>
        <p>
          We are committed to constantly refining our audio tools. If you have feature requests, notice a bug, or have ideas for new music production calculators, we would love to hear from you.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 not-prose">
          <a href="/contact/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-2.5 rounded-xl bg-neutral-900 dark:bg-neutral-100 text-white dark:text-black font-semibold text-sm hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity">
            <span>Send Us a Message</span>
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"></line>
              <polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19"></polyline>
            </svg>
          </a>
          <a href="/" class="px-4 py-2.5 rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-neutral-100 dark:hover:bg-neutral-900 transition-colors">
            Try the Tap Tempo Tool
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>

<!-- JSON-LD AboutPage Schema -->
<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "AboutPage",
  "name": "About Us - ttaptempo.com",
  "url": "https://ttaptempo.com/about/",
  "description": "Learn about ttaptempo.com, our mission to build fast, free, client-side audio utilities with zero sign-ups and zero data tracking.",
  "publisher": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "Tap Tempo",
    "url": "https://ttaptempo.com/"
  }
})} />
